Let \(X\subseteq\mathbb R^n\) be nonempty and convex, let \(f_i:X	o\mathbb R\) be convex for \(i\in I\), and let \(g_j:X	o\mathbb R\) be affine for \(j\in J\), with \(I,J\) finite. If \(\lambda\in\mathbb R_+^I\) and \(
u\in\mathbb R^J\) satisfy \(\inf_{x\in X}[\sum_{i\in I}\lambda_i f_i(x)+\sum_{j\in J}
u_jg_j(x)]>0\), then the subsystem indexed by \(\operatorname{supp}\lambda\cup\operatorname{supp}
u\) is infeasible.
